> App config settings

App config settings are settings that affect how a project is built.

These are used for features that are highly target specific, or that somehow affect the build process in some way and can't be implemented using plain Cerberus X code.

There are 3 ways to specify app config settings:

* With [[Trans]] using the command line.

* In Cerberus X source code using the preprocessor, eg: `#MOJO_AUTO_SUSPEND_ENABLED=False`. Settings made this way will not overwrite settings passed to Trans.

* By editing the CONFIG.CXS text file in your apps .build/target folder. Settings in CONFIG.CXS will not overwrite any settings passed to Trans or in Cerberus X source code, so this provides a mechanism for defining 'default' settings.

The following app config settings are currently supported:

>>> Settings for Data File Filters
Examples are shown,  actual allowable values depend on target.~n
<pre>
#TEXT_FILES="*.txt|*.xml|*.json"
#IMAGE_FILES="*.png|*.jpg"
#SOUND_FILES="*.wav|*.ogg"
#MUSIC_FILES="*.wav|*.ogg"
#BINARY_FILES="*.bin|*.dat"
#FAST_SYNC_PROJECT_DATA=True			'Set to True to enable 'fast syncing' of project data when building - warning: has problems with xcode, False by default.
</pre>

>> Setting for the Mojo module.
The defaults are shown.
<pre>
#MOJO_AUTO_SUSPEND_ENABLED=True			'Set to True to cause app to suspend when desktop window loses focus.
#MOJO_HICOLOR_TEXTURES=True	
#MOJO_IMAGE_FILTERING_ENABLED=True
</pre>

>> Settings for the C++ tool chains
The defaults are shown.~n
<pre>
#CPP_DOUBLE_PRECISION_FLOATS=False	'Set to True to enable 64 bit floats.
#CPP_GC_MODE=1  					'0 disable GC, 1=incremental collect after every OnWhatever, 2=Incremental collect every GC allocation
#CPP_GC_TRIGGER=8388608 			'Allocated memory (in bytes) before a GC 'sweep' occurs. Defaults to 8 MiB
#CPP_GC_MAX_LOCALS=8192 			'This is used with GC_MODE 2 to track local object vars and defaults to 8192
</pre>

>> Settings for the C++ Tool target
The defaults are shown~n
<pre>
#CC_OUTPUT_NAME="main_$HOST"		'Set the output name of the final executable.
#CC_OUTPUT_PATH_WINNT=""			'Set the output path for the final executable Window host. Default path is targets .build folder
#CC_OUTPUT_PATH_LINUX=""			'Set the output path for the final executable Linux host. Default path is targets .build folder
#CC_OUTPUT_PATH_MACOS=""			'Set the output path for the final executable MacOS host. Default path is targets .build folder

#CC_LINUX_CC="gcc"					'Set the C compiler to use. Linux only.
#CC_LINUX_CXX="g++"					'Set the C++ compiler to use. Linux only.

#CC_USE_MINGW="1"					'Sets the choice of compiler to use. True for MinGW, or false to use MSVC.

#CC_MSVC_TOOLSET="v142"				'Set the tool set to use for Visual Studio builds.
#CC_MSVC_WINSDK="10.0"				'Set the Windows SDK version to use. Note: 10.0 is the default to use any. 
</pre>
>> The C++ Tool compiler options
*The following configuration variables are used for backwards compatibility for MinGW and Linux GCC targets.*~n
These configuration variables are bound to makefile options.~n
*OPTS* passed to to compiler~n
*LDOPTS* and *LIBS* are passed to the linker.~n
<pre>
#CC_OPTS=""							'Pass additional gcc options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_OPTS+="-DMyDefine"
#CC_LIBS=""							'Pass additional libraries to link against for GCC type compilers.
#CC_LDOPTS=""						'Pass additional linker options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_OPTS+="-L../FILE_PATH"
#CC_MSIZE=""						'Common architecture size for MINGW and GCC. If not set, defaults to compiler default.
</pre>
*The following configuration are compiler specific. And will merge with those above*~n
These configuration variables are bound to makefile options.~n
*VPATH_OPTS* is where the make program will look for additional paths to source files.~n
*CC_OPTS* and *SRC_OPTS* passed to to compiler~n
*LD_OPTS* and *LIB_OPTS* are passed to the linker.~n
*NOTE:* To avoid issues between 64 bit and 32 bit builds. The 32 bit builds should append *_32* to each of the configuration variables ending with OPTS. 
<pre>
#CC_MINGW_CC_OPTS=""				'Pass additional MinGW options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_MINGW_OPTS+="-DMyDefine"
#CC_MINGW_LIB_OPTS=""				'Pass additional libraries to link against for MINGW type compilers.
#CC_MINGW_LD_OPTS=""				'Pass additional linker options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_MINGW_LD_OPTS+="-L../FILE_PATH"
#CC_MINGW_VPATH_OPTS=""				'Pass additional search directories for source files.
#CC_MINGW_SRC_OPTS=""				'Pass additional C++ source files to the compiler.
#CC_MINGW_MSIZE=""					'Set architecture size for MINGW. If not set, defaults to compiler default.

#CC_GCC_CC_OPTS=""					'Pass additional gcc options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_GCC_OPTS+="-DMyDefine"
#CC_GCC_LIB_OPTS=""					'Pass additional libraries to link against for GCC type compilers.
#CC_GCC_LD_OPTS=""					'Pass additional linker options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_GCC_LD_OPTS+="-L../FILE_PATH"
#CC_GCC_VPATH_OPTS=""				'Pass additional search directories for source files.
#CC_GCC_SRC_OPTS=""					'Pass additional C++ source files to the compiler.
#CC_GCC_MSIZE=""					'Set architecture size for GCC. If not set, defaults to compiler default.
</pre>
*The following are for Visual Studio installations.*~n
These configuration variables are bound to Visual Studio project properties.~n
*CC_OPTS* the C++ *AdditionalOptions* property.~n
*LD_OPTS* the Linker *AdditionalOptions* property.~n
*LIB_OPTS* the Linker *AdditionalDependencies* property.~n
*NOTES:* Targets being built against Visual Studio will produce 32 bit binaries by default. Therefore the configuration variables ending with OPTS should append *_32* to them.~n
<pre>
#CC_MSVC_CC_OPTS=""					'Pass additional MSVC options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_MSVC_OPTS+="-DMyDefine"
#CC_MSVC_LIB_OPTS=""				'Pass additional libraries to link against for MSVC compilers.
#CC_MSVC_LD_OPTS=""					'Pass additional linker options for MSVC compiler.
#CC_MSVC_MSIZE=""					'Set the CPU architecture to build for. Not setting this defaults to 32 bit.
</pre>
*The following are for Xcode installations.*~n
These configuration variables are bound to Xcode properties.~n
*CC_OPTS* are bound to the *OTHER_CPLUSPLUSFLAGS* property.~n
*LD_OPTS* are bound to the *OTHER_LDFLAGS* property.~n
*LIB_OPTS* are bound to the *OTHER_LDFLAGS* property after *LD_OPTS* configuration variable.~n
<pre>
#CC_XCODE_CC_OPTS=""				'Pass additional Xcode options for stdcpp target, eg: #CC_OPTS+="-DMyDefine"
#CC_XCODE_LIB_OPTS=""				'Pass additional libraries to link against for Xcode compilers.
#CC_XCODE_LD_OPTS=""				'Pass additional linker options for Xcode compiler.
</pre>

>> Settings for the HTML 5 target
The defaults are show.
<pre>
#HTML5_APP_FILENAME="CerberusGame.html" 'Set the default name for the html outfile. 
#HTML5_APP_ICON=""                      'set the name of a ico/png file which will be used as a favicon. If not provided, Trans will use the standard favicon.
                                        'PNG files will be converted to ICO files. Without a filepath, Trans will look in the folder where your .cxs source file is located at.
#HTML5_APP_TITLE="CerberusGame"         'Set the title inside the browser tab.
#HTML5_CANVAS_WIDTH=640                 'Set the width of the canvas.
#HTML5_CANVAS_HEIGHT=480                'Set the height of the canvas.
#HTML5_CANVAS_RESIZE_MODE=1             '0=locked, 1=stretch, 2=resize
#HTML5_CANVAS_ALPHA=False               'Set to true to enable the canvas' background alpha channel, a prerequisite for transparent canvasses.
#HTML5_CANVAS_ANTIALIAS=True			'Set to True to enable canvas anti aliasing.
#HTML5_CONSOLE_SHOW=True                'Set it to False to hide the splitter and console DIV in your file.
#HTML5_WEBAUDIO_ENABLED=True			'Set to false to disable webaudio support for mojo audio, and to use older multimedia audio system instead.
</pre>

>> Settings for the GLFW target
The defaults shown.
<pre>
#GLFW_OUTPUT_NAME="CerberuGame"			'Set the output name of the final executable.
#GLFW_OUTPUT_PATH_WINNT=""				'Set the output path for the final executable Window host. Default path is targets .build folder
#GLFW_OUTPUT_PATH_LINUX=""				'Set the output path for the final executable Linux host. Default path is targets .build folder
#GLFW_OUTPUT_PATH_MACOS=""				'Set the output path for the final executable MacOS host. Default path is targets .build folder

#GLFW_LINUX_CC="gcc"					'Set the C compiler to use. Linux only.
#GLFW_LINUX_CXX="g++"					'Set the C++ compiler to use. Linux only.

#GLFW_MINGW_STATIC=False				'Set to true will force the libraries libgcc,libstdc++ and libwinptheard to be statically linked.
										'Before doing this, check all the licencing for the MinGW distribution.

#GLFW_USE_MINGW=True					'Set to false on Windows to use MSVC instead of MinGW to build glfw apps. Needs at least VS 2015 installed.
#GLFW_GCC_MSIZE_WINNT="64"				'When building glfw apps with mingw/gcc, controls whether 32 or 64 bit apps are generated.
										'Set to "64" to force 64 bit builds on Windows (needs mingw64), or "" to use compiler default.
										'This still works for MSVC. But GLFW_MSVC_MSIZE_WINNT should be used and old sources updated.
#GLFW_MSVC_MSIZE_WINNT="64"				'Ditto but for MSVC compilers.
#GLFW_GCC_MSIZE_LINUX=""				'Ditto for Linux.

#GLFW_MSVC_TOOLSET="v142"				'Set the tool set to use for Visual Studio builds.
#GLFW_MSVC_WINSDK="10.0"				'Set the Windows SDK version to use. Note: 10.0 is the default to use the latest.
</pre>

>> The GLFW compiler options
*The following configuration variables are used for backwards compatibility for MinGW and Linux GCC targets.*~n
These configuration variables are bound to makefile options.~n
*VPATH_OPTS* is where the make program will look for additional paths to source files.~n
*CC_OPTS* and *SRC_OPTS* passed to to compiler~n
*LD_OPTS* and *LIB_OPTS* are passed to the linker.~n
<pre>
#GLFW_GCC_CC_OPTS=""					'Pass compiler options to GCC type compilers.
#GLFW_GCC_LD_OPTS=""					'Pass linker options to GCC type compilers.
#GLFW_GCC_LIB_OPTS=""					'Pass additional libraries to link against for GCC type compilers.
#GLFW_GCC_VPATH_OPTS=""				    'Pass additional virtual paths to look into when building. Currently only for GCC/MinGW compilers.
#GLFW_GCC_SRC_OPTS=""				    'Pass additional source files to be build. Currently only for MinGW/Linux compilers.
#GLFW_COPY_LIBS=""						'Copy 64bit external libraries to build directory. Currently only for Windows targets.
#GLFW_COPY_LIBS_32=""					'Copy 32bit external libraries to build directory. Currently only for Windows targets.
#
</pre>
*The following configuration are compiler specific. And will merge with those above*~n
The bindings are the same as for those previously listed above.~n
*NOTE:* To avoid issues between 64 bit and 32 bit builds. The 32 bit build should append *_32* to each of the configuration variables ending with OPTS.
<pre>
#GLFW_LINUX_GCC_CC_OPTS=""				'Pass compiler options to Linux GCC type compilers
#GLFW_LINUX_GCC_LD_OPTS=""				'Pass linker options to Linux GCC type compilers
#GLFW_LINUX_GCC_LIB_OPTS=""				'Pass additional libraries to link against for Linux GCC type compilers.
#GLFW_LINUX_VPATH_OPTS=""				'Pass additional virtual paths to look into when building. Currently only for Linux GCC compilers.
#GLFW_LINUX_SRC_OPTS=""				    'Pass additional source files to be build. Currently only for Linux GCC compilers.

#GLFW_MINGW_GCC_CC_OPTS=""				'Pass compiler options to MinGW type compilers
#GLFW_MINGW_LD_OPTS=""					'Pass linker options to MinGW type compilers
#GLFW_MINGW_LIB_OPTS=""					'Pass additional libraries to link against for MinGW type compilers.
#GLFW_MINGW_VPATH_OPTS=""				'Pass additional virtual paths to look into when building. Currently only for MinGW compilers.
#GLFW_MINGW_SRC_OPTS=""				    'Pass additional source files to be build. Currently only for MinGW compilers.
#GLFW_MINGW_COPY_LIBS=""				'Copy external libraries to build directory. Currently only for MinGW targets.
</pre>

*The following are for Visual Studio installations*~n
These configuration variables are bound to Visual Studio project properties.~n
*CC_OPTS* the C++ *AdditionalOptions* property.~n
*LD_OPTS* the Linker *AdditionalOptions* property.~n
*LIB_OPTS* the Linker *AdditionalDependencies* property.~n
*LIB_PATHS* the Linker *AdditionalLibraryDirectories* property~n
*NOTE:* It is not possile yet to pass additional source files, or search locations for sources.~n
*NOTE:* To avoid issues between 64 bit and 32 bit builds. The 32 bit build should append *_32* to each of the configuration variables ending with OPTS.
<pre>
#GLFW_MSVC_CC_OPTS=""					'Pass compiler options to MSVC compilers
#GLFW_MSVC_LD_OPTS=""					'Pass linker options to MSVC compilers
#GLFW_MSVC_LIB_OPTS=""					'Pass additional libraries to link against for MSVC compilers.
#GLFW_MSVC_LIB_PATHS=""                 'Pass a list of additional paths to search for libraries.
#GLFW_MSVC_COPY_LIBS=""					'Copy external libraries to build directory. Currently only for MinGW targets.
</pre>

*The following are for Xcode installations*~n
These configuration variables are bound to Xcode properties.~n
*CC_OPTS* are bound to the *OTHER_CPLUSPLUSFLAGS* property.~n
*LD_OPTS* are bound to the *OTHER_LDFLAGS* property.~n
*LIB_OPTS* are bound to the *OTHER_LDFLAGS* property after *LD_OPTS* configuration variable.~n
*NOTE:* It is not possile yet to pass additional source files, or search locations for sources.~n
<pre>
#GLFW_XCODE_CC_OPTS=""					'Pass compiler options to Xcode compilers
#GLFW_XCODE_LD_OPTS=""					'Pass linker options to Xcode compilers
#GLFW_XCODE_LIB_OPTS=""					'Pass additional libraries to link against for Xcode compilers.
#GLFW_BUNDLE_ID_MACOS="com.yourcompany" 'Pass the first part of an application bundle id. The name is taken from #GLFW_OUTPUT_NAME.
</pre>

*GLFW Window settings*~n
<pre>
#GLFW_WINDOW_TITLE="Cerberus X Game"
#GLFW_WINDOW_WIDTH=640					
#GLFW_WINDOW_HEIGHT=480	
#GLFW_WINDOW_RESIZABLE=False
#GLFW_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN=False
#GLFW_WINDOW_SAMPLES=0					'Set to number of samples for multi sampling (glfw3 only).
#GLFW_WINDOW_DECORATED=True				'Set to false to create a boarder less window (glfw3 only).

#GLFW_MACOS_RETINA_ENABLED=False		'Set to True to make use of the whole resolution of the Retina display. Only recommended if content is scaled accordingly and no absolute pixel coordinates are used.

#GLFW_APP_ICON=""                       'Set the name of a ico/png file which will be used as th apps icon. If not provided, Trans will use the standard icon file.
                                        'PNG files will be converted to ICO files. Without a filepath, Trans will look in the folder where your .cxs source file is located at.

#GLFW_APP_LABEL="My App"				'Human readable label for app. 
										'Must be set for cerberus://internal to map to 'per user' app data dir.
										'If not set (the default), cerberus://internal is shared by all users of app.
										'cerberus://external is ALWAYS shared by all users of app.
										'Must contain filesystem friendly chars only - generally, [A-Z], [a-z], [0-9], 
										'<space>, <underscore> <minus>, <dot> should be OK.
#GLFW_APP_PUBLISHER="My Company"		'Optional human readable publisher name for app. Must be filesystem friendly.
										'Not defined by default.
</pre>

>>> Settings for Apple iOS targets
The defaults are show.~n
<pre>
#IOS_RETINA_ENABLED=True
#IOS_ACCELEROMETER_ENABLED=True
#IOS_DISPLAY_LINK_ENABLED=True
#IOS_APP_ICON=""
</pre>

>>> Settings for Android targets
The defaults are shown.~n
<pre>
#ANDROID_APP_LABEL="Cerberus X Game"
#ANDROID_APP_PACKAGE="com.Cerberus_X.cxgame"
#ANDROID_APP_ICON=""
#ANDROID_SCREEN_ORIENTATION="user"					'"user", "portrait", "landscape"
#ANDROID_GAMEPAD_ENABLED=False
#ANDROID_ACCELEROMETER_ENABLED=True
#ANDROID_MULTISAMPLING_ENABLED=False	'If set to True, Android tries to activate 4x Multi sampling first, then 2x. 
										'If that fails it reverts back to no multi sampling. Be aware that Multi sampling slows down the rendering performance.

#ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION="16"
#ANDROID_TARGET_SDK_VERSION="28"
#ANDROID_BUILD_TOOLS_VERSION="28.0.3"
#ANDROID_GRADLE_VERSION="3.2.1"
#ANDROID_GRADLE_DISTRIBUTION="gradle-4.6-all.zip"
#ANDROID_REPOSITORIES=""
#ANDROID_JAVA_SOURCE_VERSION="VERSION_1_8"
#ANDROID_JAVA_TARGET_VERSION="VERSION_1_8"
#ANDROID_APPLICATION_EXTRAS=""

#ANDROID_VERSION_CODE="1"
#ANDROID_VERSION_NAME="1.0"
#ANDROID_NATIVE_GL_ENABLED=False					'for use with the opengl modules
#ANDROID_KEY_STORE="../../release-key.keystore"
#ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS="release-key-alias"
#ANDROID_KEY_STORE_PASSWORD="password"
#ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS_PASSWORD="password"
#ANDROID_SIGN_APP=False
#ANDROID_LOGCAT_OPTION="-s [Cerberus]:*"			'Setting this differently allows you to control the output during runtime of a connected device
</pre>

>>> Miscellaneous Settings
<pre>
'OpenGL settings. To override, set these in your code BEFORE importing opengl.gles11 or opengl.gles20
#OPENGL_DEPTH_BUFFER_ENABLED=True

'Reflection settings
#REFLECTION_FILTER=""

'Curl settings
#GLFW_CURL_STATIC=False                            'Set to true to statically link libcurl in to an executable.

'Copy licence files
#COPY_LICENCE_FILES=""							   'Use to copy any licence files. These are in the format name_COYING and name_LICENCE. 
</pre>

>>> Admob Settings
The default are shown~n
<pre>
#ADMOB_ANDROID_ADS_APPID=""										'You need to set this for the latest admob sdk
#ADMOB_PUBLISHER_ID="abcdabcdabcdabc"							'from your admob account
#ADMOB_ANDROID_TEST_DEVICE1="TEST_EMULATOR"
#ADMOB_ANDROID_TEST_DEVICE2="ABCDABCDABCDABCDABCDABCDABCDABCD"	'your device's admob ID for test mode
#ADMOB_ANDROID_TEST_DEVICE3=""
#ADMOB_ANDROID_TEST_DEVICE4=""
</pre>

Not all settings are supported by all targets, and when not supported they will silently fail.

The following config settings allow multiple values in one single line, using the "|" character as a separator.~n
(The ';' character was used in older versions and is still accepted, but it is deprecated.)

<pre>
#TEXT_FILES="*.txt|*.xml|*.json"
#IMAGE_FILES="*.png|*.jpg"
#SOUND_FILES="*.wav|*.ogg"
#MUSIC_FILES="*.wav|*.ogg"
#BINARY_FILES="*.bin|*.dat"

#GLFW_GCC_CC_OPTS=""
#GLFW_GCC_LD_OPTS=""
#GLFW_GCC_LIB_OPTS=""
#GLFW_GCC_SRC_OPTS=""
#GLFW_GCC_VPATH_OPTS=""
#GLFW_COPY_LIBS=""
#GLFW_COPY_LIBS_32=""

#LIBS=""

#REFLECTION_FILTER=""

</pre>

For the following Android settings only the "~n" character is allowed as a separator because all other charactes can be used as content:

<pre>

#ANDROID_LIBRARY_REFERENCE_1=""
#ANDROID_LIBRARY_REFERENCE_2=""
#ANDROID_MANIFEST_MAIN=""
#ANDROID_MANIFEST_APPLICATION=""

</pre>


